### Conversation / Chat API Requests
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000/api/v1
###
### NOTE: Conversations are repository-scoped (architecture Section 14) and
### require the repository to already have at least one successfully
### completed INDEX/REFRESH job (see repository.http) — otherwise streaming
### a message fails with a NotIndexedError. There is no authentication in
### the MVP, so conversations are attributed to the MVP service user
### automatically; no `userId` is accepted on the request body.

#############################################
# Variables
#############################################

@repository_id = 56d0da5b-60bb-4359-b6ad-60433bdd7ac9
@conversation_id = a34889ff-d907-49db-af22-e2313a9280fd

#############################################
# Conversation CRUD Operations
#############################################

### Create a new conversation for a repository

POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "repositoryId": "{{repository_id}}",
  "title": "Questions about the shipping module"
}

### List conversations for a repository
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations?repositoryId={{repository_id}}

### List conversations for a repository with pagination
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations?repositoryId={{repository_id}}&limit=10&offset=0

### List messages for a conversation
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations/{{conversation_id}}/messages

#############################################
# Chat (SSE streaming)
#############################################

### Ask a question in a conversation (SSE)
### Persists the user message immediately, then streams the assistant's
### answer token-by-token as `event: message` / `data: { "chunk": "..." }`
### frames, closing with `event: done`. On failure (e.g. the repository
### isn't indexed yet), closes with `event: error` instead — the user
### message is still persisted; the assistant message is only persisted if
### at least some text was generated before the failure.
###
### REST Client renders SSE as a growing response body; for a real UI, use
### EventSource / fetch+ReadableStream against this URL instead.
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations/{{conversation_id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: text/event-stream

{
  "content": "Which function calculates the shipping cost?"
}

#############################################
# Example Workflow
#############################################

### Step 1: Create a conversation for an already-indexed repository
# @name createConversation
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "repositoryId": "{{repository_id}}",
  "title": "Test conversation"
}

### Step 2: Ask a question (SSE) using the conversation ID from Step 1
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations/{{createConversation.response.body.$.data.id}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: text/event-stream

{
  "content": "What does this repository do?"
}

### Step 3: Read back the full message history
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/conversations/{{createConversation.response.body.$.data.id}}/messages
